<h2>4. ActiveCampaign</h2>

<p>ActiveCampaign has built its name on email automation, and in that specific area, it remains one of the best. The visual automation builder is intuitive, the deliverability is strong, and the segmentation tools let you get granular about who receives what message and when.</p>

<p><strong>What it does best:</strong> Email automation and segmentation. If email is the backbone of your marketing strategy, ActiveCampaign gives you more control over sequences, triggers, and conditional logic than most competitors at its price point.</p>

<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Starts at $29 USD per month, but the Lite plan is limited. Most small businesses need the Professional plan at $149 USD per month to access features like predictive sending and split automations. Pricing scales with contact count.</p>

<p><strong>Limitations:</strong> ActiveCampaign is an email-first platform that has added CRM features over time, not a true all-in-one. There is no funnel builder, no native booking system, no review management, and no SMS in the base plans. You will need to integrate third-party tools for anything beyond email and basic CRM, which brings you back to the <a href="/blog/all-in-one-vs-separate-tools">all-in-one vs separate tools</a> dilemma.</p>

<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Businesses where email automation is the number one priority and other features can be handled by separate tools.</p>

<h2>5. DUSA</h2>

<p>DUSA was built specifically for sole operators and small business teams. Not adapted from an enterprise product. Not stripped down from something bigger. Built from the ground up for the business owner who is also the marketing department, the sales team, and the customer service rep.</p>

<p>Every DUSA plan includes CRM, email marketing, SMS, a funnel and landing page builder, appointment booking, review management, pipeline management, and full automation workflows. There are no separate modules to purchase, no feature gates based on tiers, and no contact-based pricing surprises.</p>

<p><strong>What it does best:</strong> Bringing everything into one platform at a price point that makes sense for small business. Setup is measured in days, not weeks. You do not need a consultant to get started.</p>

<p><strong>Pricing:</strong> From $97 USD per month with all features included. No add-ons, no contact penalties, no separate modules.</p>

<p><strong>Limitations:</strong> DUSA is not built for enterprise-scale organisations with 100+ users. If you need multi-team permission hierarchies, custom API development, or enterprise-grade reporting dashboards, a larger platform will serve you better.</p>

<p><strong>Best for:</strong> Sole operators and small teams (1 to 20 people) who want everything in one place, operational fast, and affordable month to month.</p>

<blockquote><p>The best platform is not the one with the longest feature list. It is the one that fits the way you actually work, at a price you can sustain while you grow.</p></blockquote>

